Querying Data with PromQL
Lab Objectives
By the end of this lab, you will be able to:

Understand the fundamentals of PromQL (Prometheus Query Language)
Write simple PromQL queries to retrieve and analyze system metrics
Use Grafana's Query Editor to create visualizations with Prometheus data
Create basic dashboards displaying system performance metrics
Apply PromQL functions and operators for data manipulation
Prerequisites
Before starting this lab, you should have:

Basic understanding of Linux command line operations
Familiarity with system monitoring concepts (CPU, memory, disk usage)
Basic knowledge of time-series data concepts
Understanding of web browsers and basic networking concepts
