Task 4: Advanced PromQL Techniques
Subtask 4.1: Using Aggregation Functions
Create a new panel to practice aggregation:

Query with sum():

sum(rate(node_network_receive_bytes_total[5m]))
Query with avg():

avg(node_load1)
Query with max():

max(node_filesystem_size_bytes)
Subtask 4.2: Using Mathematical Operations
Calculate percentage:

(node_memory_MemTotal_bytes - node_memory_MemAvailable_bytes) / node_memory_MemTotal_bytes * 100
Rate calculations:

rate(node_disk_read_bytes_total[5m]) + rate(node_disk_written_bytes_total[5m])
Subtask 4.3: Using Label Matching
Exact match:

node_filesystem_size_bytes{mountpoint="/"}
Regex match:

node_filesystem_size_bytes{device=~"/dev/sd.*"}
Negative match:

node_network_receive_bytes_total{device!="lo"}
Subtask 4.4: Time Range Functions
Using range vectors:

rate(node_cpu_seconds_total[5m])
Using offset:

node_load1 offset 1h
Using increase:

increase(node_network_receive_bytes_total[1h])
Task 5: Creating Alert Rules (Optional Advanced Exercise)
Subtask 5.1: Create Alert Rules File
Create an alert rules file:

sudo tee /etc/prometheus/alert_rules.yml > /dev/null <<EOF
groups:
- name: system_alerts
  rules:
  - alert: HighCPUUsage
    expr: 100 - (avg by (instance) (rate(node_cpu_seconds_total{mode="idle"}[5m])) * 100) > 80
    for: 2m
    labels:
      severity: warning
    annotations:
      summary: "High CPU usage detected"
      description: "CPU usage is above 80% for more than 2 minutes"

  - alert: HighMemoryUsage
    expr: (1 - (node_memory_MemAvailable_bytes / node_memory_MemTotal_bytes)) * 100 > 85
    for: 2m
    labels:
      severity: warning
    annotations:
      summary: "High memory usage detected"
      description: "Memory usage is above 85% for more than 2 minutes"

  - alert: DiskSpaceLow
    expr: 100 - ((node_filesystem_avail_bytes{mountpoint="/",fstype!="rootfs"} / node_filesystem_size_bytes{mountpoint="/",fstype!="rootfs"}) * 100) > 90
    for: 1m
    labels:
      severity: critical
    annotations:
      summary: "Disk space is running low"
      description: "Disk usage is above 90%"
EOF

sudo chown prometheus:prometheus /etc/prometheus/alert_rules.yml
Subtask 5.2: Update Prometheus Configuration
Update the Prometheus configuration to include alert rules:

sudo tee /etc/prometheus/prometheus.yml > /dev/null <<EOF
global:
  scrape_interval: 15s

rule_files:
  - "alert_rules.yml"

scrape_configs:
  - job_name: 'prometheus'
    static_configs:
      - targets: ['localhost:9090']
  
  - job_name: 'node-exporter'
    static_configs:
      - targets: ['localhost:9100']
EOF

sudo systemctl restart prometheus
Troubleshooting Tips
Common Issues and Solutions
Issue 1: Services not starting

# Check service status
sudo systemctl status prometheus
sudo systemctl status node_exporter
sudo systemctl status grafana-server

# Check logs
sudo journalctl -u prometheus -f
sudo journalctl -u node_exporter -f
sudo journalctl -u grafana-server -f
Issue 2: Cannot access web interfaces

# Check if ports are listening
sudo netstat -tlnp | grep :9090
sudo netstat -tlnp | grep :3000
sudo netstat -tlnp | grep :9100

# Check firewall (if enabled)
sudo ufw status
Issue 3: No data in Grafana

Verify Prometheus data source configuration
Check that Node Exporter is running and accessible
Ensure PromQL queries are syntactically correct
Issue 4: PromQL query errors

Use the Prometheus web interface to test queries first
Check metric names using the metrics browser
Verify label names and values
Verification Steps
Verify Prometheus Installation
Access Prometheus at http://localhost:9090
Go to Status > Targets - all targets should be UP
Go to Graph and try a simple query: up
Verify Node Exporter
Access http://localhost:9100/metrics directly
You should see a long list of metrics
In Prometheus, query: node_load1
Verify Grafana Integration
Access Grafana at http://localhost:3000
Check data source connectivity
Create a simple panel with query: up
Verify data is displayed correctly
